// .github/renovate.json5
//
// AUTO-02, the declarative half of the Theia inflow (Phase 51, plan 51-01). Renovate reads this
// file from the default branch and opens one grouped pull request per Theia release.
// scripts/verify-renovate-config.mjs (the renovate-config quick row) asserts the rules below.
//
// What the file does
//  - One group, `theia`, holds every @theia/* resolutions pin in theia/package.json except
//    @theia/monaco-editor-core. The exception is a negative lookahead inside one regex matcher.
//  - @theia/monaco-editor-core has its own group, `theia-monaco-editor-core`. It keeps upstream's
//    own monaco line (1.108.201), which differs from the 1.76.0 Theia line.
//  - rangeStrategy pin on both groups: the resolutions are exact pins today.
//  - One regex customManager reads theia_release from the root configuration.toml only. Its
//    managerFilePatterns is anchored (^configuration\.toml$), and ignorePaths skips the frozen
//    configuration.toml fixture copies under .planning/. Without both, Renovate matched nine archived
//    copies and opened a Theia PR that rewrote them (BL-01). The verifier derives the tracked copies
//    with git ls-files and fails if the pattern matches any copy other than the root file.
//    configuration.toml is the single source for the Theia release this project composes. The version
//    anchor is @theia/core, because every @theia/* moves in lockstep per Theia release. One mismatch report from a real run would
//    disprove that anchor; until then it is an assumption, not a proof.
//  - The nix manager is off (Renovate's default; this file does not set it). So the Theia PR does not
//    change flake.lock, which is what AUTO-02 states (owner ruling 2026-11-03, BLOCKED.md item 5).
//    The scope rule still disables the nixpkgs input, so re-enabling nix cannot open a chore/theia-*
//    branch for it.
//  - automerge and platformAutomerge are false. The Theia PR merges only after owner review and a
//    green verify.yml.
//  - branchPrefix chore/theia-. A group branch is named by its slug, so the rendered name is
//    chore/theia-theia; the version sits in the PR title and body. The fixer class (FIX-01)
//    matches on the prefix. The first owner-dispatched live run still has to confirm the name.
//
// Checked
//  - renovate-config-validator 44.198.3, repo mode, --strict: passes.
//  - Renovate 44.198.3, local platform, dry-run=lookup, in a scratch repo with the Theia pins seeded
//    to 1.75.0 and monaco to 1.100.0: 50 upgrades to 1.76.0 on one branch, chore/theia-theia; monaco
//    to 1.108.201 on its own branch, chore/theia-theia-monaco-editor-core. Non-Theia packages
//    produced no branch.
//
// Not in this file, on purpose
//  - No cadence key of any kind. The only clock is the sweep tick plus owner dispatch (D-77).
//  - No workflow file writes. The bot App holds no Workflows permission, and no fileFilters
//    entry names .github/workflows, so a change there is never committed by this flow.
//  - No postUpgradeTasks. Renovate runs the hook in its own container clone, which has no applied
//    upstream/, so the licensing generator cannot run there (phase 51 BLOCKED.md item 18). The
//    release-train job renovate-licensing regenerates the notices on chore/theia-theia on the
//    runner after renovate-theia, and publishes the commit with scripts/publish-bump-branch.sh
//    (owner answer A4, 2026-11-04). The renovate-config row (rule no-post-upgrade) keeps the key out.
//  - No flake.lock writer is added. The Phase 52 fixer is denied flake.lock (.github/fix-gate-deny.json);
//    the nixpkgs update path stays with the owner.
//
// MEASURED (research flag F, 2026-10-31, theia dev shell, 16-core host; wall time and peak tree RSS):
//   cold yarn install --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile, empty yarn cache: 26.7 s, 488 MiB peak;
//     node_modules 688 MiB, yarn cache 1.24 GiB, so the disk need is about 2 GiB.
//   warm yarn install over an existing node_modules: 2.7 s, 395 MiB peak.
//   licensing regen (write mode, output byte-identical to the tree): 2.1 s, 186 MiB peak.
//   generate --check: 1.9 s, 158 MiB peak. The Node archive (31.6 MB) comes from the tree cache;
//     a fresh runner downloads it once.
//   The flags follow scripts/smoke-theia.sh: --ignore-scripts and PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=1. The
//     drivelist node-gyp rebuild and the browser download are outside the cold figure.
//   Runner ubuntu-latest (GitHub-hosted, about 2 GiB of disk). timeout-minutes 60, the default: the
//     cold wall is far below the 20-minute threshold that would raise it. The Renovate job runs the
//     renovatebot action, not the Mend app, so Mend's hosted limits do not apply; it is measured anyway.
//
// JSON5 subset used here: // comments, trailing commas, double-quoted strings.
{
  "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  "automerge": false,
  "platformAutomerge": false,
  "rangeStrategy": "pin",
  "branchPrefix": "chore/theia-",
  "ignorePaths": [".planning/**"],
  // WR-02: a vulnerability alert opens a chore/theia-*-vulnerability PR that bypasses the scope rule and
  // the Theia group (remediation updates are force-enabled). Security updates stay with AUTO-03.
  "vulnerabilityAlerts": { "enabled": false },
  "osvVulnerabilityAlerts": false,
  "packageRules": [
    {
      // Renovate updates everything by default. This rule turns off every dependency that is not
      // @theia/*: typescript, the @types packages, the node and yarn engines, and the nixpkgs flake
      // input. Without it those updates open chore/theia-* branches beside the Theia PR.
      "matchPackageNames": ["/^(?!@theia\\/)/"],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "matchPackageNames": ["/^@theia\\/(?!monaco-editor-core$)/"],
      "groupName": "theia",
      "groupSlug": "theia",
      "rangeStrategy": "pin"
    },
    {
      "matchPackageNames": ["@theia/monaco-editor-core"],
      "groupName": "theia-monaco-editor-core",
      "groupSlug": "theia-monaco-editor-core",
      "rangeStrategy": "pin"
    }
  ],
  "customManagers": [
    {
      "customType": "regex",
      "managerFilePatterns": ["/^configuration\\.toml$/"],
      "matchStrings": ["theia_release\\s*=\\s*\"(?<currentValue>[^\"]+)\""],
      "datasourceTemplate": "npm",
      "depNameTemplate": "@theia/core"
    }
  ]
}
